+# Account and specialist inventory — BEFORE implementation
+
+Baseline inspected: e7ecd1b72944e36481668554d05dc4e321e7b3de / tree1502404775deac8eb657d62b855bbac62aed374c. Source inspection only, not authenticated live acceptance.
+
+| Surface / state | Concrete current example | Customer gap | Proposed presentation boundary |
+|---|---|---|---|
+| `/account`, connected | “Linked Sleeper identity … (resolved, ownership not independently verified)” and “Your team: Mapped franchise” | Identity jargon leads; necessary ownership caveat is hard to parse. | “Sleeper account” / “Your team”, brief account-link limitation in optional explanation. Keep explicit lack of proof of control, no auth change. |
+| `/account/create`, `/account/sleeper` | “Create a secure DTOS identity”, “resolve your public Sleeper identity”, “resolved identity” | New customer must learn identity terminology. | “DTOS account”, “find your public Sleeper account”; plain explicit proof limitation. |
+| `/account/leagues`, import/mapping failure | “DTOS will map the franchise associated with your resolved Sleeper identity”; “Review Sleeper identity” | Internal mapping terms instead of finding team. | Describe one matching team, choose league, account review; preserve exactly-one-team guard and typed waiting/error behavior. |
+| `/account/my-dtos` | “Confirming saves only this method choice and review reference, with a new preference revision”; “Custom evidence and limitations” | Storage/version details dominate explanations. | Saved order determines personal values; clear Absolute Slot vs Relative Priced-Order in existing disclosures; confirmation retains no-order-change semantics without revision jargon. Keep all IDs/actions/API unchanged. |
+| `/front-offices`, missing competitive window | `active.executive_summary` from core says “{team} is currently classified as Unavailable …”; “Competitive Window: Unavailable” | Unknown classification becomes a franchise characterization. | Derive view-only missing summary from existing window/current facts; show “Team outlook not established” and actual reason. Keep underlying report/API unchanged, no guessed strategic state. |
+| `/front-offices`, all | Six headline profile cards, “Negotiation Style”, “Profile evidence confidence”, “Trade Compatibility”, “Show Evidence & Forecast” | Inferred/uncalibrated fit can read as intent or forecast; long heuristic prose. | Lead supported franchise facts + next action; group profile/fit evidence in disclosures, call observed activity and fit an inference. Keep score/model intact. |
+| `/fois`, retained/pending/missing | “ranked by canonical FOIS score”; “No persisted executive profiles”; “FOIS generation pending” | Specialist mechanics as normal wording. | Manager grades based on retained records; short “profiles are being prepared / not available”; keep RETAINED / NOT REVALIDATED adjacent, provenance on demand. |
+| `/fois/gms/{gm_id}` | Five technical metrics, detailed category panels and repeated qualifications in normal flow | Full evidence overwhelms decision summary. | Executive summary and retention warning remain visible; category calculations and confidence/support weights on demand. No regrading or source work. |
+| `/commissioner` | “Future explanation hook”, “Four engines / one answer”, 17 intelligence cards including unsupported values | Specialist surface exposes unimplemented hooks and unsupported models. | Remove hook placeholder; supported league overview normal, unsupported metrics and detailed source context on demand. Preserve submitted evidence/counts and all actions. |
+| `/settings` | “Application Identity”, “Provider Activation Dashboard” (already under details); raw league-setting keys | Mostly correctly optional; wording still internal. | “Application version”, “Data sources”; retain exact keys and diagnostics in details, humanize normal setting labels only. |
+| `/welcome` | Existing dark/green design, open registration, three read-only demos; no new portrait/provider claim identified | Established design should be preserved. | Audit/controls only unless a concrete internal wording defect is confirmed. |
+
+## Missing-data findings
+
+- `FO-SUMMARY`: source-to-screen presentation defect confirmed. `src/core/front_office_intelligence/engine.py:119` interpolates `Unavailable` into an executive summary that `components/front_office_intelligence.py` renders normally. Unknown model outcome must remain unknown; fix the *renderer*, not the model or report/API.
+- `COMMISSIONER-MODELS`: unsupported `future_outlook`, depth/asset-health scoring and league model values are existing analytical limitations, not lost Sleeper data. Do not fill them; stop presenting placeholder score cards as functioning everyday measures.
+- `CUSTOM-GAPS`: missing compatible Market values are deliberately qualified by the existing editor/Absolute/Relative contracts. Simplify explanation without changing availability, rank ordering, exact-pick universe or formulas.
+- `ACCOUNT-PROOF`: Sleeper public identity resolution is not proof of account control. This limitation is genuine and must remain explicit without internal jargon.
+- No confirmed acquisition/restoration/scoring loss has been established in this assigned slice. No source/provider work is justified by this audit.
+
+## Focused controls / visual plan
+
+Use actual account routes with disposable account service; complete/missing Sleeper link and league selection/mapping/waiting states. Render supported and missing Front Office profiles against same unchanged report; assert unavailable classification is not a sentence or a fabricated strategy. FOIS retained/pending/missing and profile score parity. Custom method/editor IDs/dialogs remain and original API controls run unchanged. Commissioner supported metrics versus absent model placeholders. Capture account, Custom and Front Office/FOIS at320×432,375×667,390×844,desktop through fixture browser; no physical Safari or live-owner claim. Source reads only; no provider/search/preparation on disclosures.
