+# History, picks, transactions, matchups and weekly reports — baseline inventory
+
+Baseline source: e7ecd1b72944e36481668554d05dc4e321e7b3de / tree1502404775deac8eb657d62b855bbac62aed374c. Inventory is source inspection before implementation, not an authenticated live claim.
+
+| Surface / route | Concrete normal before example | Supported states / concern | Proposed bounded presentation change |
+|---|---|---|---|
+| League History `/history` | “Immutable Sleeper evidence with season-specific settings”; “Historical standings rows”, “Blocking Issues”; primary “Open Historical API” and “Historical Coverage” JSON links | Retained season cards, archive preparation and coverage already exist | Lead with seasons/events, one plain coverage summary; developer API destinations inside optional Source details |
+| Season archive `/history/{season}` | Primary “Draft evidence (JSON)” and “Postseason evidence (JSON)” | Existing `season_archive` already supplies draft rows/brackets, champion and standings | Render retained draft selections and postseason result/bracket data directly in the existing page, with raw APIs under disclosures; no new acquisition/endpoint needed |
+| Franchise `/history/team/{id}` | Each season shows reason + activity + “19 supported source weeks” + retrieved/empty list + each gap + draft note + continuity + generation | Complete/partial/unknown retained coverage and last-valid observations available; identities qualified | Keep one visible coverage summary and season state/activity; detailed period inventory/freshness/source IDs on demand; preserve events/filter/pagination/back |
+| Historical trade `/trades/history/{id}` | Opening text describes current roster observations/as-of semantics at length; market paragraph repeats compatible/pre-trade package disclaimers | Per-asset quotes supported; package totals intentionally withheld; grades retained | Keep original exchange, movement and coverage concise, source/clock/identity and methodology details optional; material gaps remain beside the affected branch/value |
+| Picks `/picks` | “Market price: Unavailable”; “MARKET UNAVAILABLE · Unavailable · Unavailable”; “Projected range: UNKNOWN · Confidence: Unavailable · Exact slot: Unavailable” | `traded_picks` includes historical records; prepared `pick_ledger` can establish current identity/owner | One unavailable-price reason; price/source visible if supported; range unknown stated once, assumptions optional. Separate current ledger-backed rights from past/unconfirmed transfers; no claim historical pick is available to buy |
+| Pick detail `/picks/{id}` | “Consumed by verified draft conversion”, “Ownership Chain”, raw slot state; current owner observation clocks in normal flow | Conversion/exact ownership already guarded; Trade action requires current compatible ledger and unexercised right | Lead with current pick vs historical/conversion status, clear original franchise and supported action; exact IDs/clocks optional |
+| Transactions `/transactions` | Table “Timestamp”; retained archive dates raw ISO; raw source event disclosure | Completed and pending/rejected already separated | Readable UTC dates; keep raw precise timestamps in optional event source; concise action labels |
+| Matchups `/matchups` | “Technical Details”, “No canonical Sleeper projection exists for this starter” | Sleeper-only score and projection controls already present | “How this is calculated” disclosure and plain missing-projection wording, no score substitution |
+| Weekly `/reports/weekly` | “Prepared evidence for this league and week is unavailable. No result has been inferred.” and “Explore source matchup or season” | Complete, preview/live, unavailable + missing transaction evidence | “No report is ready for this week”; clear source-dependent action; keep scores/stories unchanged |
+| League `/league` | Implemented in routes/home.py | Owned by home/team agent | Coordinate; no overlapping edits here |
+
+## Source-to-screen findings, pre-implementation
+
+| ID | Field | Classification | Evidence and intended resolution |
+|---|---|---|---|
+| HL1 | Draft/postseason customer view | Existing retained evidence lost in rendering | `season_archive` supplies draft picks, brackets and placements, while primary links send users to raw APIs. Render bounded existing rows instead. |
+| HL2 | Pick unavailable source/provider/concept | Genuine missing/incompatible Market quote + repeated rendering fallback | `canonical_pick_market` appropriately returns missing price. Consolidate duplicate strings, never fabricate price or rank/range. |
+| HL3 | Historical pick availability | Historical/current identity ambiguity in normal index | Index loops `traded_picks`, even when no current `pick_ledger` proves ownership. Qualify and separate observed historical transfers from ledger-backed current rights; existing exact pick detail guards must remain. |
+| HL4 | History missing transaction weeks | Genuine unacquired/failed/unavailable coverage | Existing period and last-valid fields are available. Summarize once and retain exact weeks and clocks inside optional details; unknown never becomes no activity. |
+| HL5 | Matchup production ranks | Suspected presentation data defect, requires matched reproduction | `_production_ranks` converts absent player `points` to zero via `float(player.get('points') or 0)`. This may rank missing results as true zero. Notify root; do not change source/engine contract without a matched control. |
+
+## Regression / visual plan
+
+Reuse season archive, history coverage/follow-through, franchise progress, current-season cache restoration, exact pick/prepared page and matchup controls. Add rendered controls for direct readable draft/postseason data, partial/unknown coverage collapsed default with detailed periods still expandable, available/zero/missing pick prices and historical-vs-current rights. Capture normal theme at320×432,375×667,390×844 and desktop; long names/exact pick IDs; expand source/coverage details and verify no horizontal page overflow, keyboard focus and44px controls. Preserve RETAINED / NOT REVALIDATED, each completed/pending/rejected distinction and contextual links. Browser fixture evidence only unless an independently authorized live observation is actually made.
