+# Home and My Team before inventory
+
+Source baseline: e7ecd1b72944e36481668554d05dc4e321e7b3de / tree 1502404775deac8eb657d62b855bbac62aed374c. This is source inspection, not a new authenticated owner observation.
+
+| Route/state | Concrete before example | Customer problem | Proposed presentation only correction |
+|---|---|---|---|
+| `/` supported franchise | `Your front office`, `Assessment context and roster shortcuts`, `Explore ... Useful destinations—not personalized Attention recommendations` | Internal vocabulary competes with team name, next action and official record | Team-first header, concise roster/lineup shortcuts, factual next-action language |
+| `/` no overall model | `DTOS team assessment · not official standings`, `Projected lineups · not standings or FOIS GM rankings or an overall grade` | Repeated exclusions obscure useful weekly comparison | `Projected lineup comparison` with brief description, one overall-grade explanation inside details |
+| `/` missing weekly comparison | `Compatible weekly lineup evidence is not prepared for this league.` | User learns implementation terms, no useful state distinction | State that the week's lineup cannot yet be compared; retain precise missing evidence on demand |
+| `/` optional analytics pending/retained | `FOIS is being prepared`, `Current FOIS is unavailable` | Specialist acronym interrupts normal use | Manager-grade status in a secondary disclosure, retained status remains explicit |
+| `/teams` preseason | `Projected finish: Unavailable · Projected wins: Unavailable`; `Playoff Odds: Forecast unavailable` | Unimplemented model presented as functioning default measures | Preserve supported record/weekly comparison; omit unset forecast metrics from normal directory |
+| `/teams/{id}` roster | Every player repeats `Canonical Market: ...` | Internal term and repeated label add noise | `Market value`, keep projection/source details separately |
+| `/teams/{id}` draft capital | `Market: Unavailable · Range: Unavailable · Confidence: Unavailable` | Triple missing state repeats on every pick | One `Market price not available`; show only supported range/confidence, exact identities retained |
+| `/teams/{id}` depth | Repeated full qualification and `DTOS-derived lineup contributions`, reserve scenario technical terms | Full diagnostic explanation visible across position cards | Main position/coverage/risk visible once, full reserve and scenario evidence in native disclosure |
+| `/teams/{id}` advanced | `Advanced intelligence · Market, production and legal-lineup evidence`, per-dimension `Canonical ...` | Internal architecture presented as customer meaning | `Calculations and sources`; preserve exact diagnostic text under optional detail |
+| Home brief no preparation | `A compatible roster assessment has not been prepared for this league, week and goal` | Missing preparation risks being mistaken for weakness | Clearly separate `Your roster analysis is not ready` from a supported roster finding |
+
+## Source-to-screen findings
+
+| Case | Traced path | Classification | Resolution boundary |
+|---|---|---|---|
+| Overall score/rank unset | team intelligence overall -> directory -> Home/My Team | Deliberately unimplemented composite model, not dropped source evidence | Keep unset; explain individual strengths separately |
+| Preseason win/odds placeholders | unset team_intelligence fields -> directory default metrics | Unimplemented model exposed as normal measure | Omit unsupported metrics from everyday directory; preserve valid metrics if present |
+| Pick range/confidence missing | exact pick identity -> `pick_identity` -> My Team rows | Genuine unsupported analytical range, not verified source loss | Keep exact pick/value, omit repeated empty range/confidence labels; disclose unknown range once |
+| Prepared weekly comparison | `prepared_diagnostics` -> `prepared_comparison` -> `weekly_comparison` | Existing coherent generation/league/week/availability contract | Preserve admission and effective qualification, no recalculation/fallback |
+| Missing roster preparation | cache.peek/prepared_diagnostics -> front-office brief preparation item | Compatible evidence not prepared, not evidence of weakness | Plain pending explanation with existing safe My Team action |
+
+No confirmed ingestion/scoring/restoration defect is established by this inventory. No calculation/source/admission changes proposed. Existing rendered coverage tests include team-assessment consistency, front-office brief/workflow, My Team outlook and team-need handoff; add customer wording/disclosure regressions while preserving all their numerical and qualification assertions.
+
+## Confirmed presentation-state defect and correction
+
+Home's explicit Find Trade Ideas action previously converted the typed `trade_capacity_deferred` 503 into generic unavailability and left `data-state=loading`. The shared Trade resource policy already supplied the correct typed deferral. The Home consumer now uses that code to show waiting-for-capacity separately from actual search failure/interruption; earlier offers stay explicitly labeled as earlier results that were not updated. No admission arithmetic, retry loop, request count, evidence qualification or search implementation changes. New deterministic browser control intercepts only the response, asserts a single explicit request, truthful state, retained old cards and no raw technical error in normal text. This is a client source-to-screen state loss, not restored projection or price coverage.
+
+## Implemented boundaries
+
+- Home, `/league`, My Team and team directory copy/disclosures changed; the coherent weekly comparison function, all data models, all scoring/grade/qualification logic and source generation matching are unchanged.
+- Preseason unsupported forecast placeholders removed from the normal team directory. Real numeric probabilities, including zero, remain rendered.
+- My Team shows one unknown Market price instead of empty price/range/confidence triplets; original-franchise labels, exact pick action parameters and independently supported zero remain.
+- Depth keeps primary coverage, known points and qualification outside details; full original interpretation, eligibility and removal calculations remain inside.
+- Detailed league team-history/current-needs context is now optional; completed observed count, coverage qualification and source meaning remain visible.
+- Human timestamps on Home activity and My Team activity use the shared readable-time formatter, preserving raw clocks in existing source records.
+
+## C4 visual follow-up: repeated unknown sentinels (C5 correction)
+
+The retained C4 320px My Team screenshot showed ten repeated `Status unavailable` / `Week 1 · Sleeper Unavailable` rows, four depth cards repeating unavailable point labels, and four picks printing `Projected range: UNKNOWN · LOW`. This was a customer-visible rendering defect: known empty/model sentinel values were truthy and presented as routine measures, rather than missing data recovered from upstream.
+
+The C5 route renderer now summarizes roster projection/status/Market coverage once, with the exact player-specific gaps and original reasons in an optional list. Supported numeric projections remain on each player with their exact supplied display, including zero and negative scores. Unknown participation is stated beside any numeric projection lacking a reported status; known Out/IR/PUP and supplied bye/exclusion notes remain beside affected players. This never infers participation from an Active label or a projection. Depth keeps supported contribution/backup numbers and coverage counts; shared missing totals are named once by affected positions and exact reasons remain in position detail. Pick range UNKNOWN/empty/unavailable sentinels and their orphan confidence labels are omitted; supported ranges, exact pick identities and explicit zero Market values remain unchanged. No source preparation, scoring, admission or core data changes.
diff --git a/docs/audits/customer-experience-2252/inventory-market-player.md b/docs/audits/customer-experience-2252/inventory-market-player.md
