@@ -0,0 +1,33 @@
+# Market / player presentation inventory before implementation
+
+Baseline e7ecd1b72944e36481668554d05dc4e321e7b3de, tree1502404775deac8eb657d62b855bbac62aed374c. Source inspection only at this stage; no owner live observations or production acquisition.
+
+| Route/state | Existing concrete before example | Existing evidence and proposed presentation boundary |
+|---|---|---|
+| `/market`, complete directory | Sort choices Market / Intrinsic / Contender / Rebuilder / Confidence / Risk / Liquidity, despite unsupported modeled values. Cards already show useful identity/ownership/weekly projection/Market. | Retain usable Market ordering in normal controls; advanced existing sort choices stay optional, never invent a measure. APIs and sort semantics unchanged. |
+| `/market?selected=player:…` | “Canonical Market”, “Open canonical dossier”, “Trade Intelligence”; four metrics Market/Intrinsic/Contender/Rebuilder with repeated unavailable values, “Current market values … canonical market evidence”. | Lead with Market and Sleeper projection/results; existing model/source detail in one optional disclosure. Rename action “Open player” and use existing safe exact-player Trade action; no search on open. |
+| `/market` movement, current/sparse/incompatible | “Historical to current publication”, “retained checkpoints”, “value concept, scale, format, methodology or time ordering”, lengthy duplicated sparse-history and no-buy/sell caveats. | Keep supported change, actual date interval and source/age visible; concise compatibility gap. Exact clocks/reasons and checkpoint tables on demand. No comparison eligibility/calculation changes. |
+| `/players/{id}` | Top identity/Market/actions/Sleeper weekly projection already good. Underneath: visible Strength Analysis, Weakness Analysis, Opportunity Analysis; season/3yr/5yr entries each say no forecast. “Active Front Office”. | Keep current projection and actuals prominent; compact strengths/meaningful risks; unimplemented forecast explanation once inside optional analysis limits; “Viewing for” franchise selector. |
+| `/players/{id}` current production partial/missing | `canonical_production.production_panel` repeats a long actual-results summary, exact league and prep clocks, observation window explanations, missing score and non-Sleeper caveats. Route live panel repeats same production/projection absence in Data Availability. | One current-results answer with actual observed denominator and retained qualification beside it; windows and exact weekly coverage/source clocks optional. Preserve all numeric values, source distinction, zero/negative handling. |
+| `/players/{id}` career history | Full annual table, ownership timeline, metadata and recent transactions render after the dossier even when unrelated to current task. | Optional Career History and recent activity sections, retaining source distinctions and exact contextual Back. Ownership/chronology facts untouched. |
+| `/market` retained fallback/error | “earlier prepared publication”, “current matching replacement”, generation diagnostics on default page. | “Showing the last successful update” + brief reason; retain exact generation/freshness in optional sources. Do not call old evidence current. |
+
+## Missing-data findings (bounded source inspection)
+
+1. **Unimplemented models, confirmed:** `components/asset_intelligence.py` renders every `report.opportunity` entry (season, three/five-year horizons) even when score is None; evaluator deliberately supplies weekly-only/multi-season-unavailable explanations. No data recovery is justified. Normal presentation should stop repeating model placeholders.
+2. **Unimplemented/incomplete model measures, confirmed:** Market directory exposes Intrinsic/Contender/Rebuilder/Risk/Liquidity controls and four selected-asset model metrics even if None. Existing canonical Market and Sleeper weekly evidence are independent; no substitution or value invention.
+3. **Presentation duplication, confirmed:** `/players/{id}` renders `canonical_panel` and repeats its production summary in live Data Availability; absent NFLverse/usage/model fields remain a separate analysis limitation, not a reason to withhold an admitted explicit Sleeper score. The strict prepared-production contract remains intact.
+4. **Genuine/unprepared current result state:** `prepared_production_context` withholds mismatched/missing actual publication. No evidence in this bounded review establishes a new ingestion/restoration defect; do not introduce a fallback.
+5. **Genuine incompatible/sparse history:** trend helper explicitly preserves semantic boundaries and unknown movement. These should remain qualified with retained observations available on demand.
+
+## Owned files / coordination
+
+`routes/market.py`, `components/asset_intelligence.py`, `src/ui/canonical_production.py`, `src/ui/market_roster_relevance.py`, optional presentation text helpers and new Market/player-only tests. Player route is inside **`routes/transactions.py`**, approximately lines385–550: coordinate with History agent before editing that function; do not edit transaction/history routes elsewhere. Root owns common CSS and presentation helpers.
+
+## Planned meaningful checks
+
+Real dossier/Market TestClient fixture pages, complete/partial/missing/retained states, explicit zero and negative actuals, no unimplemented forecast cards in default-visible DOM, exact source values unchanged, actions/Market contextual Back preserved. Real Chromium at320×432/375×667/390×844/desktop using normal theme, keyboard disclosure/action focus, no overflow and default/expanded screenshots. Existing Market history compatibility and source/parity tests remain mandatory; fixtures are not live owner acceptance.
+
+## Source wording correction before final reconciliation
+
+The exact baseline opportunity labels in `player_evaluator.py` are **Current Season, 2-Year Outlook, Long-Term Outlook**. The earlier shorthand “3yr/5yr” above was inaccurate and is not a literal baseline quote. The confirmed problem is unchanged: all unsupported horizon entries render repeatedly. The new rendered control checks these exact baseline labels are absent from default-visible content. This correction does not alter a source fact or reconstruct original screenshots.
diff --git a/docs/audits/customer-experience-2252/inventory-trade.md b/docs/audits/customer-experience-2252/inventory-trade.md
new file mode 100644
index 00000000..600de90e
--- /dev/null
+++ b/docs/audits/customer-experience-2252/inventory-trade.md
@@ -0,0 +1,23 @@
+# Trade presentation inventory — baseline build2251
+
+Source e7ecd1b72944e36481668554d05dc4e321e7b3de/tree1502404775deac8eb657d62b855bbac62aed374c. Source audit before implementation, not live owner inspection.
+
+| Route/state | Concrete existing before example | Confirmed issue | Reuse/correction boundary |
+|---|---|---|---|
+| /trades, fresh not-started | "Only worthwhile bilateral opportunities", "Active Front Office" | Internal bilateral/identity vocabulary on normal entry | components/trade_intelligence.py labels only; preserve all entry URLs and source logic |
+| /trades/trade-for and /trades/shop, ready | "Find Bilateral Options" | Primary action requires internal terminology | components/trade_workspace.py: "Find offers"; same button ID/action |
+| /trades/calculator, selected package | "Advanced DTOS analysis" | Main action hides ordinary purpose | Existing #trade-run becomes "Evaluate trade"; same execution |
+| Recommended/Trade For/Shop completed current offer | offerCard adds final verdict, decisive reason/next step, acquisition roles/cost, partner/history link, send/receive, drawback, full four-line decision summary, all capital seasons/rounds, comparison button, each exact protection, every future-capital consequence and supporting paragraphs. It additionally lifts .tw-lineup-warning and .tw-lineup-details out of the main explanation into every card. | Confirmed very long default cards and duplicate risk/availability/depth text. | Reuse previewOffer(row) and preserved assessmentContext; collapsed card only decision/partner/exact package/reason/main risk/qualified active+partner current-week impact/active valuation/cost-role labels and one Review trade action. Existing details available in review without HTTP. |
+| Offer review/current | previewOffer creates "Alternative preview", repeats Original/Alternative package paragraphs, renders offerCard(row,true), then Adopt alternative/Keep original | The review uses existing persisted originalProposal/previewProposal and context; useful but wrongly framed for ordinary reviewing | Keep state/ownership/revalidation machinery; title Trade review, clarify edit/adopt versus return; group existing evidence into summary/team effects/lineups/depth/capital/sources |
+| Evaluate/current result | showEvaluation capital inventory appears before assessment and source explanation, then repeated decision/main-cost, dimensions, depth/source and rationale sections | Answer displaced by inventory and repeated warnings | Keep canonical explanation nodes, re-layer client DOM into primary summary and existing optional calculation/source groups |
+| two-offer comparison | Each alternative starts with entire capital inventory before offer heading; own/partner risk and conditions repeat; original complete assessment follows | Comparison lead obscured | Move capital into disclosure below decision/package/effects; preserve recorded baseline and compatibility checks exactly |
+| incomplete/current, retained, stale, source-changed | existing contextNotice, finalVerdict, decisionPresentation, incomplete recommendation suppression, NOT REVALIDATED semantics | Correct qualifications must remain near affected claim | No new inference/source substitution. Keep qualifications, condense duplicate presentation only. |
+| capacity-deferred/timeout/cancel/error | readiness/status feedback and late-result suppression already present | Needs plain descriptions, no false zero-offer result | Preserve typed HTTP statuses, safeguards and actual recovery behavior |
+
+## Data-path findings
+
+No confirmed lost projection/result/Market/ownership facts in this initial Trade audit. Current duplication is rendering: the same admitted decision, reserve and capital facts are appended in multiple blocks. Unsupported models/unknowns remain qualified. Any new evidence-path defect will be separately reported and matched-tested before correction; evaluator, scoring, qualification and admission remain unchanged.
+
+## Validation plan
+
+Use existing native evaluator/HTTP browser harness and prepared-offer controls. Capture exact same result payloads before/after at320×432,375×667,390×844,desktop, including long exact picks. Measure visible first-card height/text with screenshots and verify Review opens already evaluated evidence, two-sided lineups/depth/capital, comparison/return state, and zero extra API calls. Cover zero-offer/incomplete/retained/deferred/error and acquisition cost-vs-fit roles. Adapt existing tests that directly clicked details in collapsed cards to first open Review; preserve their original evidence/math assertions, focus/touch and no-new-work checks.
diff --git a/docs/audits/customer-experience-2252/inventory-visual-journeys.md b/docs/audits/customer-experience-2252/inventory-visual-journeys.md
new file mode 100644
index 00000000..676a29ab
--- /dev/null
+++ b/docs/audits/customer-experience-2252/inventory-visual-journeys.md
@@ -0,0 +1,29 @@
+# Visual and rendered journey inventory — before implementation
+
+Baseline production v1.22.36/build2251, merge e7ecd1b72944e36481668554d05dc4e321e7b3de, tree1502404775deac8eb657d62b855bbac62aed374c. Frozen premerge source9943a3c220f0064c281bc9d53803afbf1ab03f49 has this identical tree and is available as a separate read-only worktree. No production browser or owner session is used, and Opera will not be used.
+
+## Existing normal-router harness
+
+`tests/test_product_browser_journey.py` creates two disposable accounts/three league memberships, publishes three warm fixture runtimes, and traverses authentic account middleware and normal product routers using `dtos_app.page`. It forbids request-time Sleeper access and unknown external traffic, asserts legal account isolation and no runtime hydrations, and verifies cleanup. Extension hooks permit capture/audits without a second rendering system. The currently configured two viewports are1280x900 and390x844; the capture extension can use320x432,375x667,390x844,1280x900.
+
+Route inventory traversed: `/` Home; `/league`; `/teams/1`; `/fois`; `/market`; `/trades`; `/trades/create`; `/trades/trade-for`; `/trades/shop`; `/trades/recommended`; `/picks`; `/matchups`; `/matchups/1`; `/transactions`; `/players/1-QB-0`; `/front-offices`; `/settings`; `/commissioner`. Account activation, changing leagues, cross-account403, and correct primary-navigation My Team target already execute. The fixture intentionally has sparse/missing advanced evidence, so these family captures are evidence-limited rather than claims of complete owner data.
+
+## Existing actual Trade capture
+
+`/workspace/2251-trade-for-cost/styled-source-screen.py` uses authenticated loopback HTTP, native exact-target shared evaluator, full normal theme, then two-offer comparison and editable preview/return. Its exact2251 original screenshots/results exist for320/375/390/1280. This baseline is reusable unchanged. The legacy exact-target action initiates one bounded search, then an explicit Generate adds one. Comparing/opening/returning adds zero HTTP. All original2GiB enforcement/cleanup receipts are retained. Its source-tree identity matches the production baseline exactly.
+
+Concrete baseline: normal generated cards render the long decision explanation, repeated Market/availability/depth language, full two-sided consequences, draft capital and before/after lineups in repeated nested detail panels. The320px full-page native Trade screenshot is extremely tall. A fresh matched capture will record per-root-offer bounding height, visible text length, text/fonts and control geometry to compare the exact same prepared offer structure after edits. It must not count nested/exploratory `.tw-offer` elements as root result cards.
+
+## Existing specialised controls to reuse
+
+- `tests/test_my_team_intelligence_browser.py`: five sizes, roster/disclosure keyboard focus, actual roster -> player -> Back, draft capital -> exact pick -> Shop, persistent Trade draft strategy and navigation intent.
+- `tests/test_contextual_back.py`: authentic loopback HTTP redirects/static bytes, personal scope/draft/comparison/back mechanisms; no simulated auth redirect.
+- `tests/test_trade_for_acquisition_browser.py`: prepared offer role/Neutral cost/extras/FAIR-OPTIONAL fixtures, explicit Generate, editable preview, comparison, keyboard/touch, return/reload; bare component theme in original harness, so must retain normal-theme HTTP captures as visual acceptance.
+- Current baseline canonical archive retains all page-family evidence (Home/outlook, My Team, Market, player production, histories, picks/capital, Custom Absolute/Relative, welcome, account/security); exact manifests/hashes in2251 task. These remain historical source-matched controls, not freshly observed live owner pages.
+
+## Planned final acceptance
+
+1. Matched normal-router page-family screenshots at all four sizes and actual overflow/action accessibility checks, with keyboard/touch and no sticky overlap.
+2. Matched actual shared-evaluator Trade cards before/after, showing material default height/text reduction with >=existing readable text size, principal risk and Review action visible, no provider/search merely from details/comparison.
+3. New focused customer-journey test can extend existing actual-router harness with stable semantic assertions; it must not replace evaluator decisions or weaken old meaningful checks.
+4. Complete/partial/missing/retained/loading/capacity/error states should use existing native evidence fixtures and agent-focused rendered controls; each screenshot's fixture/qualification is labelled. No claim of physical iPhone/Safari or authenticated owner live acceptance.
